@startuml
!include _style.puml

title Perturbation: the profile model and what a run produces

package "Authored: what you write in the profile JSON" {

  class PerturbationProfile {
    profile_id : str
    description : str?
    default_seed : int?
  }

  class Scenario {
    scenario_id : str
    weight : float = 1.0
    description : str?
  }

  class ChainStep {
    operator_id : str
    probability : float = 1.0
    attempts : int = 1
  }

  class ExclusionRules {
    exclude_systems : tuple[str]
    exclude_countries : tuple[str]
    exclude_families : tuple[str]
  }

  PerturbationProfile "1" *-- "1..*" Scenario : scenarios\n(one is drawn per record,\nby weight)
  Scenario "1" *-- "1..*" ChainStep : chain\n(ordered)
  PerturbationProfile "1" *-- "1" ExclusionRules : exclusions
  Scenario "1" o-- "0..1" ExclusionRules : exclusions\n(replaces the profile's\nentirely, never merges)
}

package "Registered: the operator contract" {

  enum Family {
    word_order
    typo
    diacritic_punct
    legal_suffix
    phonetic
    transliteration
    low_salience
  }

  class SitedOperator {
    operator_id : str
    family : Family
    sites(name, country) : Site[*]
    change(name, site, rng, country) : str
  }

  class SitedOperatorRegistry {
    register(operator)
    get(operator_id) : SitedOperator
    list_operators() : str[*]
  }

  SitedOperatorRegistry "1" o-- "*" SitedOperator : sited_registry\n(importing operators\nregisters every family)
  SitedOperator "*" --> "1" Family
}

package "Produced: one row per record" {

  class SourceRecord {
    local_id : str
    name : str
    system : str
    country : str?
  }

  class PerturbedRecord {
    local_id : str
    name : str
    original_name : str
    scenario_id : str?
    steps_that_landed_nothing : tuple[str]
    changed : bool <<derived>>
  }

  class AppliedChange {
    operator_id : str
    family : Family
  }

  class Site {
    start : int
    end : int
  }

  PerturbedRecord "1" *-- "0..*" AppliedChange : changes\n(what actually landed)
  AppliedChange "1" *-- "1" Site : site
}

SourceRecord "1" --> "1" PerturbedRecord : always exactly one,\nchanged or not
PerturbationProfile ..> PerturbedRecord : perturb_records(records, profile, seed)
ChainStep ..> SitedOperator : operator_id, resolved\nthrough the registry
ExclusionRules ..> Family : exclude_families
SitedOperator ..> Site : sites() finds them once;\nchange() acts at one
AppliedChange ..> SitedOperator : names the operator\nthat landed it

note as N3
  **Operators own the change, the runner owns selection.**
  `apply_operator(name, operator, rng, probability, attempts)`
  calls `sites()` once, runs `min(attempts, sites)` trials that
  each draw twice, whether it fires and which site, and calls
  `change()` at every site that fired, right to left. A chosen
  site takes every site overlapping it with it. No operator
  knows how many changes were asked of it.
end note

N3 .. SitedOperator

note as N1
  **`scenario_id` is null** when no scenario applied to
  the record, and `steps_that_landed_nothing` is then
  empty. A chain that ran and landed nothing gives the
  opposite pair: a scenario id, and the steps that found
  nowhere to act.

  **`attempts` is a ceiling, not a measurement.** What a
  step achieved is the number of `AppliedChange` entries
  it contributed, which is smaller whenever a name offers
  fewer viable sites than the step asked for.
end note

N1 .. PerturbedRecord

note as N2
  **What survives to disk.** A materialized row keeps
  `scenario_id`, `original_name` and `changed`, but not
  `AppliedChange`: the operator, family and span are
  dropped, so a row records which scenario ran and
  whether the name moved, never what was done to the
  string. The run's seed is carried in the manifest and
  in every row's `system_uri` (e.g.
  `perturbed://ie/en-lite/v1/42/123`), with `source_uri`
  pointing back to the unperturbed row.
end note

N2 .. AppliedChange

@enduml
